{%- doc -%}
  Renders a hidden "Website" field that only bots fill. Render it inside a {% form %} tag that also
  renders snippets/mionas-form.liquid with `validate: true`, whose script blocks a filled submit.
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Off-screen rather than display: none, because bots skip fields a page hides outright. inert
  removes it from the tab order and from screen readers, but the browser still posts it.

  No real field uses the name contact[website]. The contact endpoint prints it in the merchant
  email, so a bot that posts without running the script still shows there.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="mionas-honeypot" inert>
  <label>
    Website
    <input
      type="text"
      name="contact[website]"
      value=""
      tabindex="-1"
      autocomplete="off"
      data-1p-ignore
      data-lpignore="true"
      data-bwignore
      data-form-type="other"
      data-protonpass-ignore="true"
    >
  </label>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .mionas-honeypot {
    position: absolute;
    left: -10000px;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
